<%#
  What a table needs from an admin and what its Sync All does (#2389, #2414):
  "3 need a decision; Sync All updates 6". Each table of Admin -> Required Pages
  draws one in its own header, beside its own Sync All button, from that table's
  counts alone: the button, this line and the toast that follows a sync all count
  the same pages.

  locals: syncSummary, one object (an include also sees its parent's data, so a
  loose name could be picked up from the screen by accident), with:
    counts  { outdatedSyncable, outdatedUserEdited } of that one table
    testId  the data-testid of the line
%>
<%
  var need = syncSummary.counts.outdatedUserEdited || 0;
  var update = syncSummary.counts.outdatedSyncable || 0;
%>
<span data-testid="<%= syncSummary.testId %>" data-need="<%= need %>" data-update="<%= update %>"><%= need > 0 ? need + (need !== 1 ? ' need' : ' needs') + ' a decision' : 'Nothing needs a decision' %>; <%= update > 0 ? 'Sync All updates ' + update : 'Sync All has nothing to update' %></span>
